-// Chapter 30 Starter: the honest output path and nothing else.
+// Chapter 30 checkpoint 1: the whole post chain runs, and every stage in it is honest about running empty.
 //
-// The scene pass publishes a scene-linear, temporally resolved display-extent baseline together with the linear
-// view depth and the Chapter 11 motion convention that the camera effects would need. The output pass then does
-// exactly one job: remove the pre-exposure, apply the camera exposure once, tone map, encode for the display, and
-// composite the UI in the domain the policy chose. There is no bloom, no motion blur, and no depth of field here,
-// and none of the helpers this file calls performs one.
+// The lab becomes the Solution variant here, so the renderer compiles and creates the camera-effect and bloom
+// pipelines and submits the stage list its validated plan declares: the scene pass, depth of field, motion blur,
+// bloom extraction, the pyramid reduction, its progressive recombination, and the output path. Every stage below
+// is a separate dispatch that reads Chain[SourceOffset + index] and writes Chain[DestinationOffset + index], so no
+// pass ever aliases its own input, publishes its own per-pixel evidence into Records, and sets its own status bit
+// only once that evidence is finite and in domain. Each one is still a pass-through: the camera effects hand the
+// radiance on unchanged and record the colour they published, the bloom stages publish an explicit zero pyramid
+// and a zero accumulator, and the output path composes, removes the pre-exposure, applies the camera exposure
+// exactly once, tone maps, encodes for the display, and composites the UI. The DofEvaluated, MotionEvaluated, and
+// BloomEvaluated flags stay clear, so no record claims an effect it did not evaluate. The displayed image is
+// therefore still the baseline, while the stage count, the stage-order word, and the status bits show the whole
+// chain executing. Each patch that follows replaces one pass-through with the algorithm it stands in for.
 #include "../Common/PostProcessingShared.hlsli"

 [numthreads(8, 8, 1)] void SceneCS(uint3 dispatchThreadId : SV_DispatchThreadID)
